  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1211 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nThanksgiving Day:\n\nThe cold conditions will continue through Thanksgiving Day.\nParticularly, morning temperatures look to start out in the low\n20s to upper teens before gradually warming up after sunrise, \nso those with any outdoor plans should make preparations for\nsome of the coldest air we've had so far this season.\nFurthermore, there is high confidence (70 to 95% chance) that\nafternoon high temperatures will remain below 50 degrees.\n\nThe Weekend:\n\nCluster analysis reveals ensembles have started to come into\nslightly better agreement with the evolution of the upper-level\npattern late this week into the weekend. That is, after a pair \nof cutoff lows eventually clear the region sometime late \nThursday or Friday, height rises will promote a warmer airmass \nbuilding over the Missouri Ozarks. Most ensemble members depict\na shortwave pivoting through the northern Plains and Upper- \nMidwest through this period, though there are differences in \njust out far south and west this disturbance intrudes. The most \nlikely trajectory of this wave would mean max temperatures in \nthe 50s and continued dry conditions. A deeper shortwave, \nconversely, would make for cooler temperatures and even open the\ndoor for some precipitation chances. This solution is low \nconfidence, however, and current PoPs remain less than 15%. \nBeyond that, there is a clearer signal for building heights and \na warming trend through the weekend.",
